).val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/152"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Middleweight (≤75 kilograms), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "9 – 23 August 2008"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/816"} "Beijing Gongren Tiyuguan, Beijing"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/258458"} "28 from 28 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The favorite was " [:a {:href "/athletes/112151"} "Matvey Korobov"] " of Russia, World Champion in 2005 and 2007. But he went out in the third round to Kazakh " [:a {:href "/athletes/106290"} "Bakhtiyar Artayev"] ", the 2004 Olympic welterweight champion. In turn, Artayev lost his next match to Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/112153"} "James DeGale"] ", silver medalist at the 2006 Europeans. Next for DeGale was his nemesis, " [:a {:href "/athletes/112888"} "Darren Sutherland"] " of Ireland, who had won four of five previous bouts against DeGale. But he lost this one, DeGale winning 10-3 to move onto the finals. There he met Cuban " [:a {:href "\\athletes\\show\\112171"} "Emilio Correa"] ", 2007 Pan American Champion, and bronze medalist in this class at the 2005 Worlds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was very close, with DeGale moving ahead early and holding on to win by a 16-14 decision. The margin was the two points Correa was penalized in the first round for biting. After the Olympics DeGale turned professional, posting a record of 12 wins and 1 loss thru April 2012. Correa’s silver medal continued the Cuban gold medal shutout in Beijing, as 2008 would mark the first time since 1968 that no Cuban won a boxing gold medal, as they won “only” four silvers and four bronzes."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {}